                <pb facs="0194" n="120" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg120"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/668</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Denmark</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Egan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-07-06T15:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 6, 1917, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 7, 12.10 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>818. <hi rendition="#italic">Deutsche Tageszeitung</hi>, July 3, quotes from a
                    speech on June 30 by Wolfgang Heine, a member of the Reichstag: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>I recently had a conversation with the Chancellor and I am in a position
                            to state that he would be willing to conclude peace towards East and
                            West to-day without any annexations or compensations. In the past the
                            Chancellor has never asserted this with such distinctness to the public.
                            He has considered it more appropriate to keep quiet. This is not owing
                            to lack of earnestness but to the nature of his position.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Egan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
